 {
  "source": "Goldman Sachs",
  "title": "Wynn Resorts Ltd. (WYNN): Takeaways from investor meetings",
  "type": "equity_research",
  "priority": "medium",
  "published": "2026-05-14",
  "insights": [
   "Goldman reiterates Buy rating and $125 price target following investor meetings in Boston and Chicago.",
   "Near-term Vegas opex is pressured by the ramp-up of new venues (Sartiano\u2019s, Zero Bond, Pisces) and upcoming Encore tower renovations.",
   "Encore renovation is characterized as defensive capex to maintain luxury status, resulting in ~80k room nights lost (5% of total) starting 2Q26.",
   "Macau's 'The Enclave at Wynn Palace' is a $900-$950mn investment designed to address capacity constraints, with 99% current occupancy.",
   "The Enclave is projected to generate ~$400mn in incremental annual GGR and $150mn-$175mn in EBITDA, implying 17%-18% ROIC.",
   "Management remains committed to dividends, noting robust cash flows are sufficient to fund both expansion and shareholder returns.",
   "UAE project (Wynn Al Marjan) remains on track with no new news since earnings; long-term guidance remains unchanged."
